/draft

# node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
.npm/

# build output
out/
dist/
release/
*.pkg.tar.zst

# makepkg's leavings, which land in packaging/ beside the PKGBUILD.
#
# The finished .pkg.tar.zst was already ignored above; everything else it drops
# was not, so the first real package build left seven untracked paths in the repo
# — build logs, namcap logs, and a 27 MB bare clone of this very repository that
# makepkg keeps as its source cache.
#
# This is I-21 again in a new place: a tool that walks into the working tree and
# leaves things behind, and a `git add -A` that would have swept them up. Named
# here rather than discovered later.
packaging/src/
packaging/pkg/
packaging/TRITIUM/
packaging/*.log

# test artefacts
coverage/
test-results/
playwright-report/
.playwright/

# editor droppings
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store

# A git worktree here holds a COMPLETE second copy of this repository, so an
# unqualified `git add -A` would commit the tree into itself. Machine-local
# settings are local by their own name. Neither is the project.
#
# .prettierignore excludes the same directory for the same reason (issues.md
# I-20); this is the other half of it (I-21). Nothing else under .claude/ is
# ignored, so a config the maker decides to track stays visible.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json
